course: dictionary
lesson: 6599
title: Noisily and noisy
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Noisily is an adverb. It tells you how an action is done, and here the action is making a lot of sound. Noisy is an adjective that describes a thing, as in a noisy room. Noisily describes how something happens, as in «the children ran noisily into the hall».
explain: Use the words around it to work out the meaning. «Elephants recognise old friends after years apart and greet them noisily with rumbles, ear flapping and trunk touches.» Rumbles are loud sounds, so noisily must mean with a lot of sound. Check it by swapping in loudly: the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Noisily can also mean with fuss, in a way that draws attention, as in «protested noisily». Here the protesters want everyone to notice them. When you meet a new meaning, put your idea into the sentence and see if it fits.
fact: Noisily is an adverb, and it tells how something is done.
fact: «Noisily» means in a loud way, making a lot of noise.
fact: «Noisily» can also mean with fuss, in a way that draws attention, as in «protested noisily».
fact: Noisy is the adjective: a noisy room, a noisy crowd.
fact: Useful phrases: chew noisily, slurp noisily, noisily slammed.
exercise: «The children ran noisily into the hall.» How did the children run? | Quietly on tiptoe | Backwards | Slowly and sadly | *Loudly, making a lot of noise
exercise: Nadia says noisily is just another word for noisy. What is the difference? | *Noisy describes a thing, and noisily describes how something is done | Noisily is a noun and noisy is a verb | There is no difference at all | They mean opposite things
exercise: «Elephants greet them noisily with rumbles.» Find and copy the adverb that tells how the elephants greet. | elephants | trunk | rumbles | *noisily
test: «He slurped his soup noisily.» What does noisily mean here? | Very slowly and politely | *With a lot of sound | Happily, with a smile | Without any soup at all
test: Please don't move ___ in the library. Which word fits the gap? | happiness | noise | noisy | *noisily
exam: The crowd protested noisily outside the town hall. What does noisily suggest? | Quietly and calmly | Sleepily | Without any words | *Loudly, with fuss that draws attention
